    {
      "id": "claim_12cc87d81a754cfcac116f305f5f6a3a",
      "statement": "For each citation, _validate_citation looks up the resolved doc_id only among the documents actually retrieved for the current turn (_find_document_by_id scans retrieval_results.results[*].docs), so a citation can never validate against a document that was not retrieved this turn even if it exists elsewhere in the corpus.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/validation_citations.py#L147-L203",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9be958440f035848629c36bc596147c5c8fd892da9eb69c10e7a691c51f43f4e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b4106a59a4eb47459a91b0e98de666d9",
      "statement": "_verify_quote accepts a citation's quote if it is an exact substring of the cited document's content, or if fuzzywuzzy.process.extractOne(quote, [document_content], score_cutoff=threshold) returns a non-None match; the threshold is a caller-supplied parameter of structure_and_validate_async defaulting to 85, and the graph's validate_answer node always calls it with quote_match_threshold=85. An empty quote or empty document content always fails.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/graph/nodes/generate.py#L80-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc5947d811b1abfac4d469796f593722b00274caa94ec799cd6d35332d44e107:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/validation.py#L43-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1d34cac50831cc470f1faefc605b7b0aef2f5bae6513ca2dfaa781b6cdb7e824:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/validation_citations.py#L205-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:312785519c1da54f6411060fcb0fc858769e8d0f3ebd0878a970ecd06da07aa8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_978c0f4464a84e73b24d02f4e225bf1c",
      "statement": "Fuzzy quote verification scores the quote against the entire document content string rather than a specific sentence or span, so a textually similar but non-supporting or even contradicting quote can pass at or above the threshold; it only checks citation-to-source-text similarity, not statement entailment, factual/medical correctness, or whether the citation points at the semantically right (versus merely textually similar) retrieved document.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/validation_citations.py#L205-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:312785519c1da54f6411060fcb0fc858769e8d0f3ebd0878a970ecd06da07aa8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_59de64d35336439cb48f9c5d9a9a19f6",
      "statement": "A statement with citations survives only if at least one citation passes verification (failed citations are individually dropped from a surviving statement); a statement with zero citations is treated as automatically valid and kept without any fuzzy verification; a statement whose citations are all invalid is dropped entirely.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/validation_citations.py#L95-L138",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2b7d83b02f12dc64ab9ee77da2a72a2a2da9de937324368207e28781c2b6e61c:"
        }
